<http://data.silknow.org/object/cc54d5e4-65ec-3ada-8509-eecde4b413d5/observation/2>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The pocket gave its name to some other portable accessories such as the pocket book or pocket case and to the pocket-handkerchief.  Richly decorated pocket and letter cases were part of the oeuvre of eighteenth century domestic embroidery.  They were often made in silk, and beautifully embroidered with silk or silk ribbon and metal threads."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cc54d5e4-65ec-3ada-8509-eecde4b413d5> .

